<title>CHINA: Esprit Holdings shrs ease after JV news.</title>
<headline>Esprit Holdings shrs ease after JV news.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Esprit Holdings Ltd were easier on Friday around midday following news that the company intended to form a joint venture in China with China Resources Enterprise Ltd, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There was some profit-taking after the news since it is not certain what will the changes be after the formation of the joint venture, which would make and distribute consumer goods,&quot; said Charles Cheung, executive director at J &amp; A Securities.</p>
<p>The stock eased HK$0.30 to HK$5.30 after retreating from a morning high of HK$5.90. It had surged steeply recently on hopes that China Resources would buy into the company.</p>
<p>-- Hong kong Newsroom (852) 2843 67369</p>
</text>
